WEBVTT

00:09.657 --> 00:12.497
Master!

00:39.977 --> 00:43.597
<i>If Perugius hadn't shown up when he did,</i>

00:43.597 --> 00:46.727
<i>I might never have seen 
any of them again.</i>

00:49.117 --> 00:51.857
Rudy? What's wrong?

00:54.487 --> 00:56.127
You're safe now.

01:08.037 --> 01:09.037
Zanoba.

01:09.397 --> 01:10.607
Master!

01:10.977 --> 01:13.207
Have your injuries healed?

01:13.207 --> 01:16.487
Yes. What about yours, Zanoba?

01:16.487 --> 01:18.207
Yes. See for yourself.

01:18.527 --> 01:21.737
Sorry my spell got you, too.

01:21.737 --> 01:24.747
I'm sure you did what you thought best.

01:24.747 --> 01:28.827
Now, let us celebrate our safe return.

01:28.827 --> 01:30.127
Good idea.

01:30.567 --> 01:33.857
Now if Nanahoshi gets better, 
all's well that ends well.

01:33.857 --> 01:35.707
Nanahoshi's fine.

01:35.707 --> 01:38.557
She's more or less stabilized.

01:39.067 --> 01:42.407
I'm more worried about Cliff now.

01:42.407 --> 01:44.607
Is it the demon eye you 
got from Kishirika?

01:44.607 --> 01:45.627
Yeah.

01:45.977 --> 01:48.667
She said it's called the 
Eye of Discernment.

01:49.117 --> 01:52.227
It shows information 
about everything I see,

01:52.227 --> 01:54.257
so it's like there's writing everywhere.

01:54.747 --> 01:58.757
I ran into the same problem right 
after I got my demon eye.

01:58.757 --> 02:01.417
Oh, I'll get it under 
control soon enough.

02:01.767 --> 02:05.527
You can count on me if anything 
like this comes up again.

02:05.887 --> 02:06.867
I will.

02:06.867 --> 02:09.977
If you're thinking of dropping 
in on Nanahoshi, go ahead.

02:10.327 --> 02:12.227
She should still be awake.

02:12.227 --> 02:14.707
Good. I'll go see her.

02:17.127 --> 02:24.007
<b>III</b>

02:17.127 --> 02:24.007
<b><i>Mushoku Tensei</i></b>

02:17.127 --> 02:24.007
<b><b><i>Jobless Reincarnation</i></b></b>

02:34.107 --> 02:35.807
How are you doing?

02:36.427 --> 02:38.197
I feel much better.

02:38.607 --> 02:42.457
They told me I need another 
month of rest, though.

02:43.377 --> 02:46.807
Thank you for doing what you did.

02:48.267 --> 02:52.167
I heard you went to a dangerous 
place just to get me this medicine.

02:52.527 --> 02:55.567
I, um, appreciate it.

02:55.927 --> 02:58.327
<i>She's sure on her best behavior.</i>

02:58.627 --> 03:00.027
It's no big deal.

03:00.387 --> 03:06.987
Looking back, I've been awfully cavalier 
with you, even though you're older.

03:06.987 --> 03:08.497
I'm sorry about that.

03:08.497 --> 03:10.077
Don't sweat it.

03:10.077 --> 03:12.177
I'm only 18 here.

03:12.467 --> 03:14.547
May I ask how old you were before?

03:14.547 --> 03:19.177
Thirty— Nah, let's not talk about age.

03:19.177 --> 03:21.037
You don't have to act all polite, either.

03:21.037 --> 03:22.707
Let's keep things how they've been.

03:23.127 --> 03:24.017
All right.

03:28.327 --> 03:31.477
I'm sure you heard, but your condition...

03:31.477 --> 03:33.927
Won't ever go away. I know.

03:35.657 --> 03:40.497
<i>The sokas grass can temporarily 
purge the mana from her body,</i>

03:40.497 --> 03:43.627
<i>but it will eventually build up again.</i>

03:43.957 --> 03:48.747
<i>She can't live in this world 
and avoid contact with mana.</i>

03:50.237 --> 03:53.917
Nanahoshi, you've got to get home.

03:53.917 --> 03:56.047
You shouldn't have to die in this world.

03:57.587 --> 03:58.747
Right.

03:58.747 --> 04:01.047
I'll do whatever I can to help.

04:08.677 --> 04:10.927
Thank you.

04:14.157 --> 04:16.787
I'm going home.

04:16.787 --> 04:20.657
Sure you are. 
I bet you can't wait to get back.

04:20.657 --> 04:24.877
No, I mean I won't be able to 
repay all I owe you before I do.

04:24.877 --> 04:27.267
Forget about owing me anything.

04:27.267 --> 04:31.457
Oh, but I'd appreciate it if you'd 
give me advice when I need it.

04:32.207 --> 04:33.467
All right.

04:35.897 --> 04:37.867
That's that, then.

04:37.867 --> 04:39.087
Take care of yourself.

04:39.487 --> 04:42.387
I will. Thank you so much.

04:44.467 --> 04:50.597
And then my master unleashed 
violet magic that scorched Atofe.

04:50.597 --> 04:55.737
Oh? Then it was his arts 
that left Atofe so weak.

04:55.737 --> 04:58.527
And what happened then?

04:58.527 --> 05:02.497
Well, I lost consciousness 
at that point, so—

05:02.497 --> 05:04.247
You're all having tea?

05:04.247 --> 05:06.737
Master! Yes, indeed!

05:06.737 --> 05:11.497
King Perugius wished to hear 
of our battle with Atofe,

05:11.497 --> 05:14.527
so I was just regaling 
him with the details.

05:14.527 --> 05:16.367
I've heard how you fought, Rudeus.

05:16.567 --> 05:21.477
It seems it was your magic that left 
Atofe in such a weakened state.

05:22.497 --> 05:25.757
I can still see the 
ridiculous figure she cut.

05:25.757 --> 05:28.587
<i>Does he hate her guts that badly?</i>

05:28.587 --> 05:30.177
You seem pleased.

05:30.177 --> 05:35.547
I wasn't expecting to stumble upon 
an opportunity for vengeance.

05:35.547 --> 05:37.537
Vengeance, sire?

05:37.537 --> 05:38.787
Yes.

05:38.967 --> 05:43.307
She put me through hell 
many a time in the Laplace War.

05:43.307 --> 05:46.217
I had planned to even the 
score one of these days,

05:46.217 --> 05:52.527
but my friend North God Kalman forbade 
mortal combat between me and Atofe.

05:52.527 --> 05:56.667
Before I knew it, I had lost my chance 
for revenge and half given up hope.

05:57.107 --> 06:00.547
I never dreamed she would 
strike the first blow.

06:00.857 --> 06:05.507
I must thank you. Well done.

06:05.507 --> 06:08.567
You don't mind breaking your word?

06:08.567 --> 06:11.187
Kal forbade <i>mortal</i> combat.

06:11.187 --> 06:15.037
He wouldn't object to 
a one-sided beating.

06:15.037 --> 06:17.947
And it will take more 
than that to kill her.

06:19.877 --> 06:23.397
It seems I've somewhat misjudged you.

06:23.397 --> 06:26.837
I must give you some reward.

06:26.837 --> 06:28.117
A reward...

06:30.637 --> 06:36.367
Would you, uh, be willing to 
teach me some combat techniques?

06:37.637 --> 06:42.427
Did Atofe spark something in you? 
Or have you grown greedy?

06:42.427 --> 06:47.937
No, it's just... I was thinking I'd like 
the strength to keep my family safe.

06:49.817 --> 06:53.807
I will give you a means to contact me.

06:54.137 --> 06:55.537
Sylvaril.

06:58.407 --> 07:01.597
Use that in a place with ties to me.

07:01.597 --> 07:06.167
Clearnight will hear, 
and Almanfi will come for you.

07:06.907 --> 07:10.787
<i>Is the idea that he'll bail 
me out when I need it?</i>

07:10.787 --> 07:15.617
Sit with us. 
Surely there is more to be said.

07:16.487 --> 07:21.207
<i>Perugius turned out to be a 
cool guy once you got to know him.</i>

07:21.547 --> 07:25.337
<i>I didn't know enough to follow 
a lot of what he said,</i>

07:25.687 --> 07:29.337
<i>but just listening to him 
got me feeling curious.</i>

07:29.337 --> 07:35.397
Sire, we are thinking of selling my 
master's figurines in the near future.

07:35.397 --> 07:38.357
Would you give us the benefit 
of your frank opinion?

07:40.077 --> 07:44.567
You ask this knowing my 
hatred for demonkind?

07:44.567 --> 07:48.237
I should have known you would be 
able to tell at a glance, sire.

07:48.707 --> 07:53.437
<i>Zanoba ought to know Perugius can't 
stand demons as well as I do.</i>

07:53.437 --> 07:54.907
<i>What's his angle?</i>

07:54.907 --> 07:58.867
You would sell a thing like this? 
Think better of it.

07:59.197 --> 08:05.017
But sire, you yourself are indebted 
to the model of this piece.

08:05.017 --> 08:06.377
Me, in his debt?

08:10.187 --> 08:13.887
You don't mean that this 
is Ruijerd Superdia?

08:13.887 --> 08:16.117
Precisely so.

08:16.117 --> 08:19.617
You graciously recounted the 
final battle with Laplace to me.

08:19.957 --> 08:25.497
In it, this same Ruijerd came to the 
aid of you and your companions.

08:25.757 --> 08:31.747
Naturally, I quite understand your 
distaste for demonkind, sire.

08:31.747 --> 08:37.407
But my master's craft will cause a stir 
in the art world if it becomes known.

08:37.407 --> 08:39.827
Wouldn't you like to see that?

08:39.827 --> 08:43.047
To see a wonderful world 
awash in works of art?

08:43.047 --> 08:48.407
I detest the Superd. They slaughtered 
the innocent without exception.

08:48.407 --> 08:53.427
Still, my life would have been 
forfeit if not for Ruijerd.

08:53.787 --> 08:56.617
And yet... Hm...

08:57.267 --> 09:01.947
Sire, Ruijerd regrets what he's done.

09:01.947 --> 09:03.577
Does he?

09:03.577 --> 09:10.327
Laplace manipulated him into dishonoring 
his people and killing his own family.

09:10.327 --> 09:11.837
Laplace, was it?

09:12.237 --> 09:17.827
He hates Laplace, and he's traveling the 
world to restore his people's good name.

09:18.167 --> 09:21.587
These figures will help 
him in that quest.

09:21.887 --> 09:24.837
Would you give your 
blessing for his sake?

09:25.267 --> 09:29.407
The Superd's honor means nothing to me.

09:30.037 --> 09:33.227
Still, I must pay my debts.

09:33.227 --> 09:35.347
You mean...

09:35.347 --> 09:36.947
Do as you please.

09:37.347 --> 09:39.427
Thank you for your kindness.

09:39.427 --> 09:42.447
My thanks, sire!

09:40.047 --> 09:44.577
<i>That's another step toward 
rehabilitating the Superd's reputation.</i>

09:44.957 --> 09:47.197
<i>Just you wait, Ruijerd.</i>

09:47.197 --> 09:48.687
Oh, yes. Master.

09:48.687 --> 09:52.657
Why don't you show King Perugius 
how you craft your figurines?

09:52.657 --> 09:54.347
How I make figures?

09:54.347 --> 09:55.727
Why not?

09:55.727 --> 09:58.037
Your magic intrigues me.

09:58.527 --> 09:59.787
Very well.

10:03.077 --> 10:04.947
Is that Sylvaril?

10:05.377 --> 10:10.287
I'm astonished anyone has turned 
earth magic to such a purpose.

10:10.287 --> 10:13.577
I'll make anything you 
care to commission.

10:13.577 --> 10:17.817
Will you? If you make something 
of quality, bring it to me.

10:17.817 --> 10:19.687
I will buy it from you.

10:19.687 --> 10:21.237
If that interests you,

10:21.237 --> 10:25.477
the Asura Kingdom boasts 
fine stonemasons as well.

10:25.477 --> 10:30.427
I will have a statue made in your 
honor when I ascend the throne.

10:31.277 --> 10:36.307
I care nothing for statuary made 
only to satisfy your vanity.

10:37.497 --> 10:41.757
Surely you will have more pressing 
concerns if you claim the throne?

10:42.167 --> 10:43.877
W-Well...

10:46.187 --> 10:48.257
Ariel Anemoi Asura,

10:48.627 --> 10:51.537
what is a king to you?

10:51.537 --> 10:54.747
What do you think 
"a true king" signifies?

10:54.747 --> 10:56.337
Well...

10:56.667 --> 11:02.067
A knowledgeable king who heeds ministers, 
understands their station, and...

11:02.067 --> 11:03.287
I think not.

11:03.777 --> 11:09.877
My friend Gaunis Freean Asura was a 
true king, but he was nothing like that.

11:10.257 --> 11:15.467
He was a cowardly man, 
averse to battle,

11:15.467 --> 11:17.657
and fond of ogling barmaids.

11:18.267 --> 11:22.317
But he possessed the most 
important quality of a king.

11:22.677 --> 11:27.487
I consider him a true king 
for that reason.

11:28.337 --> 11:30.617
What is that vital quality?

11:30.617 --> 11:35.277
If you can tell me in your own words, 
I will lend you my aid.

11:35.987 --> 11:39.547
<i>I get it. He's testing Ariel.</i>

11:39.777 --> 11:43.357
Rudeus, do you know what it is?

11:43.357 --> 11:46.077
You mean, what makes a king?

11:48.437 --> 11:50.087
Personally...

11:50.687 --> 11:56.197
I'd like a king who puts themselves 
in their subjects' shoes.

11:56.197 --> 11:57.237
Oh?

11:57.987 --> 12:01.407
This man gave a better 
answer than you did.

12:03.137 --> 12:07.327
Think on it, Ariel Anemoi Asura.

12:11.787 --> 12:16.147
The most important quality 
for a king to have...

12:20.407 --> 12:22.007
We're back!

12:22.007 --> 12:24.857
Coming! Welcome home!

12:25.857 --> 12:28.237
Big Brother! Sylphie!

12:28.237 --> 12:29.147
We're home.

12:29.147 --> 12:30.967
Is it over?

12:30.967 --> 12:33.397
Did you save Nanahoshi?

12:33.717 --> 12:34.797
Or—

12:34.797 --> 12:36.657
Welcome back, both of you.

12:37.057 --> 12:38.407
Nice to see you.

12:38.407 --> 12:41.327
Are you feeling all right, Sylphie?

12:41.327 --> 12:44.797
Yup. Sorry for leaving 
you to hold the fort.

12:44.797 --> 12:46.087
I don't mind.

12:46.087 --> 12:50.447
The original plan was for 
me to come home sooner.

12:50.957 --> 12:54.227
I'm guessing it all worked out, then?

12:54.227 --> 12:57.457
Yeah. I'll fill you in later.

12:57.457 --> 12:59.337
But first...

13:01.537 --> 13:02.677
It's good to be home.

13:04.617 --> 13:06.107
It's good to have you back.

13:09.317 --> 13:12.917
And so, Nanahoshi will be fine for now.

13:13.317 --> 13:18.757
But all we found out about Mom's 
condition is that it's probably a curse.

13:19.097 --> 13:20.227
Sorry.

13:20.537 --> 13:23.207
Even that is a big step forward.

13:23.487 --> 13:28.637
I'd like to keep visiting the 
flying fortress and looking for a cure.

13:28.637 --> 13:33.127
I think I'll be away for a bit, too,
 guarding Princess Ariel.

13:33.377 --> 13:34.727
I understand.

13:34.727 --> 13:36.707
Don't worry about things here.

13:37.007 --> 13:38.227
Sorry.

13:38.227 --> 13:40.957
I'll come back home any day I can.

13:40.957 --> 13:42.887
Keep an eye on Lucie for me.

13:42.887 --> 13:45.927
I will see to any domestic matters.

13:45.927 --> 13:47.467
I appreciate it.

13:49.047 --> 13:52.977
And that's my report. I'll let you 
know if anything new comes up.

13:57.747 --> 14:03.537
<i>A lot's happened in the short time 
since we went to see Perugius.</i>

14:03.917 --> 14:06.887
<i>Nanahoshi collapsed, we went 
to the Demon Continent,</i>

14:06.887 --> 14:09.857
<i>met Kishirika, pissed off Atofe...</i>

14:12.437 --> 14:14.027
She sure was strong.

14:16.187 --> 14:19.627
I'd better toughen up a little myself.

14:20.187 --> 14:26.007
<i>In that sense, learning from Perugius 
should be a move in the right direction.</i>

14:27.047 --> 14:29.927
And... what else was there?

14:31.197 --> 14:36.307
<i>I've got so much to think about, 
I'm forgetting the older stuff.</i>

14:36.307 --> 14:39.957
<i>I'll wind up repeating old 
mistakes if this keeps up.</i>

14:40.547 --> 14:42.907
I know. I'll keep a diary.

14:42.907 --> 14:45.877
<i>Now to get writing. 
No time like the present.</i>

14:57.747 --> 14:58.757
There.

15:00.677 --> 15:02.797
<b>Diary</b>

15:00.677 --> 15:02.797
<b>Rudeus Greyrat</b>

15:03.347 --> 15:06.067
Now, where should I start?

15:06.957 --> 15:09.667
<i>How long has it been 
since I've kept a diary?</i>

15:09.677 --> 15:16.737
<b>Today I decided to start keeping a diary of...
Anyway, these past ten days have been...</b>

15:10.277 --> 15:13.107
I hope I actually stick 
with it this time.

15:23.327 --> 15:24.287
Hi!

15:24.947 --> 15:26.157
You again?

15:26.877 --> 15:29.667
I guess that means I dozed off.

15:29.667 --> 15:31.127
Long time no see.

15:31.127 --> 15:36.837
I spent three years adventuring, 
and you never showed up once.

15:36.837 --> 15:39.747
I mean, I know I wasn't 
exactly at my best.

15:39.747 --> 15:40.977
You've got that right.

15:40.977 --> 15:45.847
On the other hand, 
you've really been riding high lately.

15:45.847 --> 15:49.767
Well, yeah. I got married, 
and I have a loving family.

15:49.767 --> 15:53.367
I've got it so good, my last 
life can't begin to compare.

15:53.767 --> 15:56.347
You even got to know Perugius.

15:56.347 --> 15:59.377
Oh, Perugius? He sure is something, huh?

15:59.377 --> 16:01.447
And Atofe took a shine to you.

16:01.447 --> 16:05.497
You know, I really wish she hadn't.

16:05.497 --> 16:09.747
I'd have been in trouble if Roxy hadn't 
taught me king-class water magic.

16:09.747 --> 16:12.787
True enough. That spell blew me away.

16:12.787 --> 16:18.637
It's not every day you see magic ignore 
battle aura and paralyze the flesh.

16:18.637 --> 16:21.087
Battle aura? What's that?

16:21.337 --> 16:26.097
A way to use the mana in your body 
to boost your physical abilities.

16:26.097 --> 16:32.237
Mastering it makes you move faster, 
and it takes a lot to hurt you.

16:32.237 --> 16:36.447
People tell me it comes naturally 
when you train your body.

16:36.447 --> 16:40.977
I've been keeping in shape, but I've 
never pulled off something like that.

16:40.977 --> 16:42.877
It happens.

16:42.877 --> 16:46.187
Some people can't generate aura, 
no matter how hard they train.

16:46.437 --> 16:48.207
It comes down to talent.

16:48.617 --> 16:50.267
Thanks for the heads up.

16:50.267 --> 16:52.197
Don't let it get you down.

16:52.197 --> 16:58.297
You've got magic that can ignore aura. 
It should even work on Orsted.

16:58.297 --> 16:59.877
Would it really?

16:59.877 --> 17:02.967
Hey, I don't want to start 
anything with Orsted.

17:02.967 --> 17:04.567
I've got no beef with him.

17:04.567 --> 17:05.727
You don't say.

17:05.727 --> 17:09.427
That reminds me. I owe you for Begaritt.

17:09.797 --> 17:12.537
I can't pretend I don't have regrets,

17:12.537 --> 17:17.557
but it worked out, even though 
I didn't take your advice.

17:17.557 --> 17:20.227
Well, it was your choice.

17:20.227 --> 17:25.047
Out of curiosity, what would've 
happened if I hadn't gone?

17:25.047 --> 17:26.287
If you hadn't gone,

17:26.287 --> 17:31.447
your father would have found a way 
to rescue your mother without dying.

17:31.447 --> 17:38.097
And you would have claimed both 
beast princesses and lived happily.

17:38.447 --> 17:40.177
You're kidding.

17:40.177 --> 17:43.387
You mean Paul died because I joined him?

17:43.617 --> 17:45.057
You got it.

17:45.057 --> 17:51.627
It went bad because you were there and 
he tried to show off for you, remember?

17:51.957 --> 17:55.137
Hang on. But, I mean...

17:55.137 --> 17:59.397
He would have rescued your mother 
if you'd left him to it.

17:59.397 --> 18:01.417
Roxy, too, of course.

18:02.257 --> 18:04.737
That's kind of hard to believe.

18:04.737 --> 18:07.027
It's too good to be true, you know?

18:07.027 --> 18:11.317
Maybe. But that's fate for you.

18:11.587 --> 18:13.267
Yeah?

18:13.267 --> 18:15.887
So, it would've gone better without me.

18:16.377 --> 18:19.577
Damn it. Hearing that gets me down.

18:19.877 --> 18:21.487
It's water under the bridge.

18:22.357 --> 18:25.837
I guess you're right. 
Regrets won't change anything.

18:26.277 --> 18:28.887
I feel happy right now.

18:29.247 --> 18:33.337
Maybe I made the wrong choice, 
but that's a fact.

18:33.697 --> 18:37.847
The way I see it, 
it wasn't all bad for me.

18:37.847 --> 18:39.307
Ever the optimist.

18:39.817 --> 18:42.477
By the way, what's up today?

18:42.477 --> 18:44.547
Have you come to give me more advice?

18:44.547 --> 18:48.167
Nah, more like to ask you a favor.

18:48.167 --> 18:50.367
A favor? That's new.

18:50.367 --> 18:53.357
Even I need a favor 
every once in a while.

18:53.787 --> 18:55.337
Well, okay, I guess.

18:55.337 --> 19:00.577
I've been thinking it wouldn't hurt to 
just take your advice once in a while.

19:00.577 --> 19:02.027
What, really?

19:02.027 --> 19:04.047
I'm glad to hear it.

19:04.047 --> 19:06.767
I mean, you have helped me out a bunch.

19:06.767 --> 19:09.587
If anything, I'm sorry 
I doubted you before.

19:09.587 --> 19:12.107
I am a god, you know?

19:12.107 --> 19:15.637
I like to think I don't get 
my kicks swindling people.

19:15.877 --> 19:17.017
Fair.

19:17.407 --> 19:19.727
So, what do I need to do?

19:19.727 --> 19:21.317
It's nothing major.

19:21.847 --> 19:26.687
I'd like you to pop down to your basement 
and check for anything unusual.

19:26.687 --> 19:30.227
If you don't find anything, 
then that's that.

19:30.227 --> 19:33.157
Unusual how? Why?

19:33.537 --> 19:35.367
No, got it.

19:35.367 --> 19:39.267
I'll do it without asking 
questions this time.

19:40.107 --> 19:41.487
Is that so?

19:47.447 --> 19:49.407
Thanks.

20:00.227 --> 20:02.497
Did Sylphie or Roxy cover me?

20:03.367 --> 20:05.407
They should've woken me up.

20:11.367 --> 20:12.987
<b>Diary</b>

20:11.367 --> 20:12.987
<b>Rudeus Greyrat</b>

20:12.977 --> 20:14.497
Now—

20:15.467 --> 20:17.227
It's freezing.

20:17.697 --> 20:20.987
I'm supposed to check 
the basement, right?

20:20.987 --> 20:23.047
Weird advice, but oh well.

20:23.977 --> 20:27.527
Don't tell me something 
happened to our holy relics.

20:27.527 --> 20:29.537
No, no way that's it.

20:41.467 --> 20:43.117
Must've imagined it.

20:45.517 --> 20:47.327
Or so you think!

20:47.747 --> 20:48.967
Yeah, right—

20:53.267 --> 20:56.357
Did I... succeed?

20:57.887 --> 21:01.237
No. A failure, I see.

21:01.907 --> 21:04.587
Of course it wouldn't work.

21:04.587 --> 21:06.237
Wh-Who are you?

21:07.527 --> 21:10.177
Is that you, Man-God?

21:12.697 --> 21:15.307
Don't go to the basement.

21:15.307 --> 21:18.587
The Man-God has tricked you.

21:18.587 --> 21:22.807
Hold on. Who are you?

21:22.807 --> 21:24.717
How did you get in here?

21:25.867 --> 21:27.077
I am...

21:29.807 --> 21:31.477
My name is...

21:37.207 --> 21:41.647
<i>It was a name no one in this 
world but me would know.</i>

21:42.447 --> 21:46.317
<i>A name I was going to take to my grave.</i>

21:46.957 --> 21:49.107
<i>A name I didn't even want to remember.</i>

21:49.697 --> 21:52.777
<i>The name of someone who 
doesn't exist in this world.</i>

21:53.547 --> 21:57.257
<i>It was my name in my previous life.</i>

21:58.067 --> 22:01.697
I've come from the future.

22:02.007 --> 22:05.007
<b>Episode 11
Turning Point 4</b>

23:35.027 --> 23:40.027
Next Time
An End and a Beginning
